    {
      "horseName": "doitnow",
      "winTips": 1,
      "winTotal": 8,
      "winPerc": 13,
      "ewTips": 0,
      "ewTotal": 5,
      "ewPerc": 0,
      "napTips": 0,
      "napTotal": 1,
      "napPerc": 0,
      "expertCount": 1,
      "commentCount": 1,
      "comment": "Do It Now is a 3-year-old colt trained by Adrian Paul Keatley. He was quite a precocious 2-year-old, finishing 2-3-1 in his first three starts as a 2-year-old. He trotted up by 4.5 lengths over today's trip at Ripon and opened on a mark of 87. In previous races, he got beat 1.75 lengths behind Barrak in a class 2, who's not run since. The runner-up, Station X, a half-length ahead, finished his campaign by winning his last two races in 2-year-old nurseries, posting a career-high RPR of 86. Adrian Paul Keatley has his yard in good form, with 4 out of 10 wins in recent weeks, winning with his last two starters, Kihavah and Romieu. So it could be a good time to catch Do It Now on seasonal reappearance at a very appealing 18-1 off a mark of 80 with Oisin McSweeney claiming 3lb."
    },
    {
      "horseName": "emeraldarmy",
